This repository includes third-party software:

- Desktop UI (`packages/app`, `packages/desktop`, `packages/ui`,
  `packages/session-ui`, `packages/util`): forked from
  [opencode](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode) (MIT).
- Agent kernel, from [pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi) by
  Mario Zechner (MIT):
  - `packages/ai`, `packages/agent`, `packages/chord`,
    `packages/telemetry`: vendored from pi, hash-locked against
    `upstream-lock.json`, unmodified (see `UPSTREAM.md`).
  - `packages/kernel/src/host`, from snapshot `f8f75544b` (2026-07-13):
    `host/system-prompt.ts` and `host/resources.ts` derive from pi
    `packages/coding-agent`; the embedded-debugging domain code
    (toolchain, examples index, logic analyzer, oscilloscope) is
    Yoma's own. The retired tool implementations in
    `packages/kernel/attic/` (`read`/`bash`/`edit`/`write`,
    `edit-diff`, `path-utils`, `file-mutation-queue`) also derive
    from pi `packages/coding-agent`
    (see `packages/kernel/UPSTREAM.md`).
- `engines/stm32-config-kernel`: STM32 configuration / codegen kernel.
  `data/*.irpack` is a **build artifact**: parse the local STM32CubeMX
  device database with `stm32ck-import` (`npm run engines:build` does this).
  Packs are not committed. ST HAL / CMSIS sources (`data/fw/`, ~1.1GB)
  are also not in this repository; fetch them locally with
  `tools/fetch-fw.ps1` if you need the compile-gate tests.
- `engines/controller_map`: board netlist pin extraction.
- `packages/kernel/src/host/domain/scope/{analyze,limits,siglent}.ts`:
  measurement algorithms (histogram base/top, span-averaged frequency),
  Siglent memory-depth / sample-rate tables and command-timing values
  were ported as ideas from
  [ngscopeclient / libscopehal](https://github.com/ngscopeclient/scopehal-apps)
  (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) Andrew D. Zonenberg and contributors).
  No source was copied; see `docs/scope-drivers.md`.
- `packages/kernel/test/fixtures/examples/cube-mini`: a stub
  fixture that mimics an STM32Cube tree layout. It is not ST HAL source.

See `LICENSE` for the MIT text that covers this repository.
